1. Vendored OOLONG scoring code

   File:     bench/oolong/vendor/oolong_eval_helpers.py
   Origin:   https://github.com/abertsch72/oolong, path src/eval/eval_helpers.py,
             commit 0bb7eabe839218fee7fe8d007f41cfc2fd3ae24c
   License:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Amanda Bertsch
             (full text in bench/oolong/vendor/LICENSE.oolong)
   sha256:   247583a3b653b91c39fb88a102460802f1493175b23d05a7217aead0d685c64c

   The file is a byte-identical copy so that ASSAY's OOLONG scores are
   computed by the benchmark's own code. It is loaded through
   bench/oolong/scorer.py with its heavy dependencies stubbed. It is not
   modified. bench/oolong/vendor/PROVENANCE.md records the pin.

2. OOLONG corpus packs

   Files:    bench/oolong/packs/corpus_spam4k.txt, corpus_spam8k.txt,
             questions_spam4k.jsonl, questions_spam8k.jsonl (the two smoke
             packs), and manifest_*.json for every pack.
   Origin:   derived from the OOLONG dataset (oolongbench/oolong-synth) at
             the revision pinned in each pack's manifest, by
             bench/oolong/packs/build_pack.py.
   Terms:    the dataset's own terms apply to the text (see the upstream
             dataset card named in the manifests). These files are not covered
             by the Apache license above.

   Only the two smoke packs ship. The length-ladder packs (synth128k,
   synth1m, synth4m) are manifests here: their text is rebuilt on the user's
   machine from the pinned revision with `build_pack.py fetch` and never
   enters this repository. A manifest carries no dataset text.

3. The journal standard, the independent checker and the evidence packs

   Files:    verify/ (assay_verify.py, JOURNAL_SPEC.md, CLAIM_GRAMMAR.md,
             README.md) and evidence/ (the published journals, their heads
             and the pack notes)
   License:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Mohsen Arjmandi (verify/LICENSE), so
             that anyone can verify a journal without a license to the
             harness. They moved here from the retired assay-verify
             repository in 1.1.0. The checker shares no code with src/assay
             (tests/test_verify_independence.py).

No other third-party source is vendored. Python dependencies (numpy, pillow,
pytest, and the benchmark client libraries) are installed from their own
distributions under their own licenses and are not included here.
